# Machine-local build configuration for the Makefile.
# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust the values for your machine.
# `.env` is gitignored — keep personal / machine-specific values there, not in the repo.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Consumed by `make signed`, which builds VoiceInk and re-signs it with a real
# code-signing identity so macOS TCC grants (Accessibility, etc.) survive rebuilds.

# Code-signing identity used by `make signed`.
# This string is matched as a regex against `security find-identity -v -p codesigning`.
# Use an identity name or an exact 40-char SHA-1 hash. Examples:
#   SIGN_IDENTITY=Apple Development
#   SIGN_IDENTITY=Developer ID Application
#   SIGN_IDENTITY=AB12CD34EF...   (exact certificate SHA-1)
SIGN_IDENTITY=Apple Development
